{"id":"word:hebrew:H517","type":"word","title":"אֵם","subtitle":"H517 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a mother (as the bond of the family); in a wide sense (both literally and figuratively [like father])","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אֵם (H517) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 220 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אֵם (ʼêm) means a mother (as the bond of the family); in a wide sense (both literally and figuratively [like father]) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 2 26."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אֵם","transliteration":"ʼêm","pronunciation":"ame","strong":"H517","lemmaId":"hebrew:H517","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["אִמּ֔/וֹ","אִמּֽ/וֹ","אִמּ֑/וֹ","אֵ֥ם","אִמֶּֽ/ךָ"],"morphs":[["HNcfsc/Sp3ms",79],["HNcfsc/Sp2ms",25],["HNcfsc/Sp1cs",23],["HNcfsc",15],["HC/Ncfsc/Sp3ms",14],["HR/Ncfsc/Sp3ms",8],["HNcfsa",8],["HC/R/Ncfsc/Sp3ms",6],["HNcfsc/Sp3fs",5],["HC/Ncfsc/Sp1cs",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"a mother (as the bond of the family); in a wide sense (both literally and figuratively [like father])","usage":"dam, mother, × parting.","full":"H517. em אֵם 221 noun feminine mother (Phoenician אם , Arabic , Ethiopic , Sabean אם (only in proper names compare e. g. Bae Rel 118 ) Assyrian ummu COT Gloss ; Aramaic אִימָּא אֵם, , ) — ׳א absolute Gen 32:12 +; construct 3:20 +; suffix אִמִּי 20:12 + etc.; plural only suffix אִמֹּתֵנוּ Lam 5:3 ; אִמֹּתָם Jer 16:3 ; Lam 2:12 (twice in verse); &#8212; 1 literal (human) mother , as parent Gen 20:12 ; 32:12 ; 44:20 ; Exod 2:8 ; Psa 51:7 ; 113:9 ( opposed to עֲקֶרֶת ) Jer 15:8 , 10 ; 20:14 ; 22:26 ; 50:12 ; 1Chr 4:9 ; Song 6:9 ; 8:5 +; hence of Eve כָּלחָֿ֑י אֵם Gen 3:20 ; in poetry of birth, אֵם מִבֶּטֶן יָצָא Job 1:21 ; Eccl 5:14 ; אֵם מֵרֶחֶם יָצָא Num 12:12 compare Psa 139:13 ( Jer 20:18 &) גּוֺזִי אִמִּי מִמְּעֵי Psa 71:6 (subject ׳י , compare גחה 22:10 ; &gt; גּוֺזִי = my benefactor from birth Thes Ew Hup Pe); also קִבְרִי אִמִּי וַתְּהִי Jer 20:17 ; אֵם מִבֶּטֶן = from earliest existence Judg 16:17 ; Job 31:18 ; Psa 22:11 ; so אֵם מִמְּעֵי Isa 49:1 ; as giving suck Song 8:1 ( אֵם שְׁדֵי ) Psa 22:10 ; compare 131:2 (see Exod 2:9 compare 2:8 ); as exercising authority Gen 21:21 ; 24:28 ; 27:11 , 13 , 14 ; Judg 17:2 f Ruth 1:8 ; Song 3:4 ; 8:2 etc.; especially of queen-mother as possessing dignity & influence 1Kin 1:11 ; 2:13 , 19 , 20 ; 2Chr 22:2-3 , Song 3:11 ; Prov 31:1 ; compare names of mo-thers of kings of Judah 1Kin 14:21 , 31 ; 15:2 , 10 , 13 +; as shewing love & care 1Sam 2:19 ; 1Kin 3:27 ; 17:23 ; 2Kin 4:30 ; Isa 66:13 (simile of ׳י s comforting his people; compare also Gen 27:45 ); as beloved & lamented 1Kin 19:20 (|| אָב ) Gen 24:67 ; Psa 35:14 ; בֶּןאִֿמּוֺ = own (uterine) brother Gen 43:29 ; & || אָח 27:29 ; Deut 13:7 ; Judg 8:19 ; Psa 50:20 ; 69:9 ; Song 1:6 ; compare 8:1 ; so בַּתאִֿמּוֺ Lev 18:9 ; 20:17 ; Deut 27:22 (|| בַּתאָֿבִיו ) Gen 20:12 ; often with אָב , as parentes Jer 16:3 ; Zech 13:3 (twice in verse); Isa 8:4 ; as rightfully claiming honour, authority, etc., compare above, Gen 28:7 (P) compare 37:10 (E) Judg 14:2 f, so in precept Prov 1:8 ; 6:20 ; 10:1 ; 15:20 etc. compare Ezek 22:7 ; laws enjoining these Exod 20:12 = Deut 5:16 ; Lev 19:3 compare Deut 22:15 ; laws prohib. contrary Exod 21:15 , 17 (E) Lev 20:9 (twice in verse) (H) Deut 21:18-19 , 27:16 ; laws as to mourning for Lev 21:2 , 11 (H) Num 6:7 (P) compare Jer 16:7 ; Ezek 44:25 ; left for wife Gen 2:24 ; for mother-in-law Ruth 2:24; for husband Deut 21:13 (law for captive women); compare 33:9 (of devoted service of Levites); loving, caring for children Prov 4:3 (on the opposite compare Psa 27:10 ); loved, cared for Josh 2:13 compare 2:18 ; 6:23 . 1Sam 22:3 ; 1Kin 19:20 compare 2Sam 19:38 . 2 figurative of Deborah as caring for her people בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל אֵם Judg 5:7 (compare אָב Isa 22:21 ; Job 29:16 ); so of a city 2Sam 20:19 ('stock, race, community' RS K 28 compare Proph. iv. n 8 ); of Israel Hosea 2:4 ; 2:7 ; 4:5 ; compare 10:14 ; of Judah Isa 50:1 (twice in verse); of Hittite as mother of Jerusalem חִתִּית וְאִמֵּךְ הָאֱמֹרִי אָבִיךְ Ezek 16:3 , 45 compare 16:44 ; 16:45 ; also 19:2 , 10 & see 23:2 . 3 of animals , dam Exod 22:29 (of ox & sheep) Lev 22:27 (of bullock, sheep, or goat); Exod 23:19 = 34:26 = Deut 14:21 (of kid); mother-bird 22:6 (twice in verse); 22:7 ; figurative Job 17:14 ׃ לָרִמָּֽה וַאֲחֹתִי אִמִּי אָ֑תָּה אָבִי קָרָאתִי לַשַּׁחַת . 4 = point of departure or division הַדֶּרֶךְ אֵם Ezek 21:26 . (|| הַדְּרָכִים שְׁנֵי ראֹשׁ ).","rootNote":"a primitive word;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 2 26","keyReferences":["1Chr 2 26","1Chr 4 9","1Kgs 1 11","1Kgs 2 13","1Kgs 2 19","1Kgs 2 20","1Kgs 2 22","1Kgs 3 27"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":220,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 2 26","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֥ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 4 9","book":"1Chr","chapter":4,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אִמּ֗/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncfsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 11","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 2 13","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 2 19","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/אֵ֣ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncfsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 2 20","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אִמִּ֔/י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsc/Sp1cs"},{"reference":"1Kgs 2 22","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/אִמּ֗/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncfsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 3 27","book":"1Kgs","chapter